---
title: Document ingestion — runtime flow
---
sequenceDiagram
    %% Author: YottaDynamics | Scope: read_document runtime behavior in this PR
    %% Purpose: Explain default-on ingestion, PDF subprocess dependencies, and optional table extraction.

    actor Model as Model / user
    participant Tool as ReadDocumentTool<br/>internal/agent
    participant Paths as ValidateReadPath<br/>credential deny-list
    participant Registry as documents.Registry
    participant Native as Native extractors<br/>CSV/JSON/XML/HTML/XLSX/DOCX/PPTX
    participant PDF as PDFExtractor<br/>pdftotext + optional tables
    participant Sandbox as Sandbox<br/>host or podman
    participant Helper as extract_pdf_tables.py<br/>pdfplumber

    Model->>Tool: read_document(path, caps)
    Tool->>Paths: ValidateReadPath(path)
    Paths-->>Tool: allowed or credential-path error
    Tool->>Registry: Lookup(path extension)

    alt pure/native formats
        Registry->>Native: Extract(request with caps)
        Native-->>Tool: metadata + capped sections + warnings
        Tool-->>Model: structured result
    else PDF
        Registry->>PDF: Extract(request with caps)
        PDF->>Sandbox: pdfinfo path
        alt pdfinfo fails
            PDF->>PDF: add warning: page count unavailable
        else pdfinfo succeeds
            Sandbox-->>PDF: total page count
        end
        PDF->>Sandbox: pdftotext -layout -f start -l end path -
        alt encrypted PDF
            PDF-->>Tool: warning result, no text extracted
            Tool-->>Model: structured warning result
        else pdftotext missing or fails
            PDF-->>Model: actionable pdftotext error
        else plain text succeeds
            Sandbox-->>PDF: page text
            PDF->>PDF: build page sections under max_chars
            opt optional table tier
                PDF->>Helper: ResolveScript(extract_pdf_tables.py)
                Helper-->>PDF: host cache path or in-image path
                PDF->>Sandbox: python3 extract_pdf_tables.py path --start --end
                alt python3/pdfplumber/helper unavailable or malformed output
                    PDF->>PDF: silently skip table sections
                else table extraction succeeds
                    Sandbox-->>PDF: JSON pages/tables/rows
                    PDF->>PDF: append page N table M sections
                end
            end
            PDF-->>Tool: metadata + page sections + optional table sections
            Tool-->>Model: structured result
        end
    else unsupported extension
        Registry-->>Model: unsupported format error
    end
